  "acceptance_criteria": [
    "The responsive patient home presents synthetic Maria's infusion tomorrow, its countdown or time proximity, current readiness state, and a clear action to begin the readiness check.",
    "Completing the readiness check with a cancelled ride and patient-reported clinical concern creates exactly one navigation task and one clinical-review task from genuine local application state.",
    "The clinical concern remains visible verbatim, routes to a named human-controlled pathway through deterministic logic, and is never presented as AI diagnosis, triage, or treatment advice.",
    "The staff exception queue and Maria case workspace show treatment risk, reason, owner, due time, current state, next action, and prior activity without dead controls in the primary journey.",
    "The Treatment Readiness Graph visibly anchors both blockers to the upcoming infusion and updates consistently as staff acknowledge the clinical task and confirm simulated transportation.",
    "Ana's caregiver view receives only Maria-authorized transportation status and exposes no clinical-concern detail.",
    "Maria can acknowledge the confirmed plan, after which both blockers have defined dispositions, the readiness state becomes plan confirmed, and the append-only event timeline reflects the complete causal sequence.",
    "A one-click reset restores the deterministic opening state; refresh either restores current local state or safely reinitializes without breaking the scripted demonstration.",
    "Every intended surface is visually complete at mobile and presentation-laptop sizes, keyboard operable, visibly focused, non-color-dependent, and equivalent under reduced motion.",
    "All people, resources, delivery, protocols, outcomes, Ochsner/FHIR connections, and staff identities shown in the product are clearly synthetic or simulated, and the required frontend build and critical-path smoke commands pass."
  ],
